WEBVTT

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:04.480
Every Monday morning, the public settings of more than

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:09.040
ten thousand domains in the six Arabian Gulf states are read,

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:12.870
just as any visitor on the internet sees them.

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:16.800
This is the Gulf Cybersecurity Baseline:

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:19.280
an independent, open source measurement

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:22.160
that publishes the Arabian Gulf as a whole,

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:24.160
and a page for each state,

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:28.550
without naming any organisation or ranking the states.

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:33.760
Thirteen standards, from email spoofing protection and signed DNS,

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:36.960
to post quantum key exchange.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:41.120
Every figure can be quoted as it stands, in Arabic and English,

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:45.760
with its issue number, and a link back to the very same figure.

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:49.520
And you can check your own domain now, from your browser.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:53.150
Nothing you type ever reaches the site.

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:56.270
The Gulf Cybersecurity Baseline.

